-- title:
--   Fibration of the GL₃ Whittaker block over bottom rows
-- statement:
--   Fix a homomorphism $\omega$ from the ideles of $\mathbb{Q}$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, reals $a,b$, a set $\Phi_0\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A})$ and a finite set $S$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$. Then there are a subgroup $P\le\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A})$, a measure $\nu$ on the space of orbits of $N\cap P$ (the subgroup [`WhittakerBlock.unipotentSubgroup3`](def/LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_WhittakerBlock.html#L15), generated by the matrices `upperUnipotent3 x y z`, intersected with $P$) acting on $P$, and a map $s:\mathbb{A}^3\to\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A})$ with the following seven properties. Write $e_3=(0,0,1)$, $R_S$ for the set of $x\in\mathbb{A}^3$ arising as the bottom row of the chosen representative `q.out` of some $q$ in [`WhittakerBlock.zerothShell S`](def/LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_WhittakerBlock.html#L34), $dx$ for the product of three copies of adelic additive Haar measure, $W_f$ for `whittaker3` formed with `psiQ` and with the pins `productionPinsOf ℚ ∅ (fun _ => ⊥) (fun _ => 1) (AdelicBox.adelicBox ℚ)` (so its inner integrations use additive Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box), and call $\Phi:\mathbb{A}^3\to\mathbb{C}$ admissible when $\Phi(x)=\prod_i\Phi_i(x_i)$ with each $\Phi_i$ in [`NumberField.AdelicFourier.pureTensorSet`](def/NumberField_AdelicFourier.html#L75) and factorizable and standard outside $S$, $\Phi$ takes nonnegative real values, and $\int\Phi>0$. (1) For every $F$ in `cuspFunctions ω a b Φ₀` (an element of `automorphicSubmodule ω a b Φ₀` that is continuous and cuspidal along $P_{21}$ and $P_{12}$) and every admissible $\Phi$, the block [`WhittakerBlock.block`](def/LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_WhittakerBlock.html#L40) at $\sigma=1$ and level $S$ equals $\int^{}_{R_S}\|\Phi(x)\|\bigl(\int\|W_{F\cdot s(x)}(q)\|^2\,d\nu(q)\bigr)dx$, all integrals being lower Lebesgue integrals in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}_{\ge0}$. (2) $s$ tends to $1$ as $x\to e_3$. (3) Every neighbourhood of $e_3$ meets $R_S$ in a set of positive measure. (4) For every continuous $F$ invariant on the left under $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$ and on the right under the image of `localMaximalCompact3` at each $p\notin S$, and every $C\ne\infty$: if the fibred integral above equals $C\cdot\int\|\Phi\|$ for all admissible $\Phi$, then the fibre integral $\int\|W_{F\cdot s(x)}(q)\|^2\,d\nu(q)$ is almost everywhere equal to a constant $C_1$ on $R_S$. (5) $g\in P$ if and only if the bottom row of $g$ is $e_3$. (6) For $x\in R_S$ and $p\notin S$, the $p$-component of $s(x)$ lies in `localMaximalCompact3`. (7) There are a measure $\mu_P$ on $P$, right-invariant, positive on open sets and finite on compacta, and $c_0\ne0,\infty$, with $\nu=c_0$ times the pushforward under the quotient map of $\mu_P$ weighted by the density [`HaarQuotient.density`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L25) for $N$ with its measure `unipotentHaar3`, multiplied by the indicator of the set of $g$ whose component at each $p\notin S$ lies in `upperUnipotent3`-matrices times `localMaximalCompact3`.
--
--   This is the fibration of the $\mathrm{GL}_3$ Whittaker block at exponent $\sigma=1$ over the bottom rows of the zeroth shell, together with an explicit description of the fibre data: the mirabolic-type group of matrices with last row $e_3$, a section $s$ integral outside $S$, and a weighted right-invariant measure on the fibre. It is used to produce a right translate with non-vanishing $L^2$ inner product, in [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_inner_toL2_translateRight_ne_zero_of_forall_whittakerBlock_one_mul_eq`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_inner_toL2_translateRight_ne_zero_of_forall_whittakerBlock_one_mul_eq).
